course: dictionary
lesson: 15294
title: Playful words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like a game, but they are real words with real meanings. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «The fox saw the dogs and skedaddled into the bushes.» The dogs are a threat and the bushes are a place to hide, so skedaddled must mean ran away fast.
explain: Skedaddle is informal and playful, so it sounds lively rather than serious. «Now skedaddle, all of you, before Mum sees the mess!» Here it means leave quickly. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "Now run off quickly, all of you" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Skedaddle is a verb, so it changes its ending: skedaddles, skedaddled, skedaddling. «Yesterday the cat skedaddled off the sofa when the vacuum started.» The -ed ending shows it happened in the past, and the context tells you what the cat did.
fact: Skedaddle is a verb: skedaddles, skedaddled, skedaddling.
fact: «Skedaddle» means to run away quickly, often because you are frightened or caught.
fact: «Skedaddle» can also mean to leave a place in a hurry.
fact: It is an informal, playful word, often used in stories and family talk.
fact: «Skedaddle» came into English in the USA in the 1860s, and it is used in the UK, Australia and elsewhere too.
exercise: «The sneaky squirrel skedaddled up the tree when the dog barked.» What does skedaddled mean? | Fell asleep | *Ran away quickly | Ate slowly | Sang loudly
exercise: Mum shouts, «Skedaddle, the bus is coming!» What is Mum asking you to do? | Wait for a letter | Read a long book | *Hurry off right now | Sit down and rest
exercise: «The mice skedaddled under the floorboards.» Which word tells you what the mice did? | *skedaddled | floorboards | mice | under
test: «After the thunder started, the campers skedaddled back to their tents.» What does skedaddled mean? | Went to sleep | Built a big fire | Stayed by the fire | *Hurried away quickly
test: Which playful, informal word means to leave a place in a hurry? | Admire | *Skedaddle | Pause | Stroll
exam: «The goats skedaddled when the farmer came in, and the gate swung shut behind them.» What is a good meaning for skedaddled? | Stood very still | *Ran off quickly | Slept in the barn | Asked for help
